Krita Nova 55 - three-finger drag changes brush size and opacity

New canvas input action "Brush Size and Opacity" (KisBrushSizeOpacityGestureAction,
Configure Krita > Canvas Input Settings), on a three-finger drag in every
bundled input profile ([Brush Size and Opacity] 0={0;4;[];0;0;8} -
ThreeFingerDrag, which no profile used):

- the first 12 px of movement decide the direction for the rest of the drag;
- up / down: brush size, on a log scale (150 px doubles / halves it), 1 to
  10000 px;
- left / right: opacity, 400 px for 0 to 100 %, at least 1 %;
- the value shows in a floating message on the canvas (a new one only when
  the shown text changes);
- applied at most every 30 ms (the last value always, also when the fingers
  stop or lift): every change updates the preset, the toolbar sliders and the
  brush outline, which could not keep up with every touch event;
- through the canvas resources (KoCanvasResource::Size / Opacity), like the
  toolbar sliders.

A three-finger tap stays Redo. Profiles the user has customized (saved in
the resource folder) need the gesture added in Canvas Input Settings.
